{
  "id": "shannon-communication-channel-tec",
  "name": "Capped-service message processing with illustrative losses",
  "description": "Illustrative continuous-stock message-processing compartment with capped service and two cumulative outcome counters. Queue Q receives 50 messages per arbitrary time unit; service is min(Q,60), implicitly using a one-time-unit first-order processing scale below the cap, not an instantaneous-work-conserving queue. Outcomes use a fixed illustrative fraction 0.5*exp(-(10/2)/2); the Signal_Power, Noise_Power and SNR labels are legacy knobs for that chosen fraction, not calibrated physical channel measurements. This is not an M/M/1 queue, Shannon capacity calculation, bit-error model, coding theorem or stochastic packet simulation. Fractional messages are fluid quantities. The default Euler step is 0.5; mathematical balances are tested, not empirical performance. Formerly Shannon Communication Channel Model; the Shannon1948 citation did not establish these service/loss equations. Original equation provenance is unverified. Existing IDs, equations, inputs, diagram and outputs are retained for compatibility.",
